{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\n\ndef convert(value) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a complex, int, or float number to polar coordinates (r, theta).\n    r is the magnitude and theta is the phase angle in radians.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(value, (complex, int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a complex, int, or float number.\")\n\n    if isinstance(value, complex):\n        re = value.real\n        im = value.imag\n    else:\n        re = float(value)\n        im = 0.0\n\n    r = math.sqrt(re * re + im * im)\n    theta = math.atan2(im, re)\n\n    return (float(r), float(theta))"}
