{"task_id": "Mbpp/270", "solution": "def _is_even_index(index):\n    \"\"\"Checks if an index is even.\"\"\"\n    return index % 2 == 0\n\ndef _is_even_value(value):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is an even number.\"\"\"\n    return value % 2 == 0\n\ndef _iterate_and_accumulate(lst):\n    \"\"\"Iterates through the list, applies parity checks, and accumulates qualifying values.\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for index, value in enumerate(lst):\n        if _is_even_index(index) and _is_even_value(value):\n            total_sum += value\n    return total_sum\n\ndef sum_even_and_even_index(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of even numbers at even positions (0-based) of a list.\n    Delegates to internal helpers for iteration and parity checks.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _iterate_and_accumulate(lst)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/271", "solution": "def even_Power_Sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Compute and return sum of first n even natural numbers each raised to the 5th power.\n    Returns 0 when n is 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        even_number = 2 * i\n        total_sum += even_number ** 5\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/273", "solution": "def _validate_tuple_type(x: object, name: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Raises TypeError if x is not a tuple.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(x, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(f\"Input '{name}' must be a tuple.\")\n\ndef _validate_lengths_equal(a: tuple, b: tuple) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Raises ValueError if the lengths of tuples a and b are not equal.\"\"\"\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\ndef _validate_numeric_elements(t: tuple, name: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Raises TypeError if any element in tuple t is not an int or float.\"\"\"\n    for i, element in enumerate(t):\n        if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in tuple '{name}' must be numeric (int or float), but element at index {i} is {type(element).__name__}.\")\n\ndef _compute_elementwise_subtraction(a: tuple, b: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Computes the element-wise subtraction of two tuples.\"\"\"\n    return tuple(x - y for x, y in zip(a, b))\n\ndef substract_elements(a: tuple, b: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Subtracts the elements of the second tuple from the first tuple element-wise.\n    Performs validation for tuple types, equal lengths, and numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_tuple_type(a, 'a')\n    _validate_tuple_type(b, 'b')\n    _validate_lengths_equal(a, b)\n    _validate_numeric_elements(a, 'a')\n    _validate_numeric_elements(b, 'b')\n    return _compute_elementwise_subtraction(a, b)"}
