{"task_id": "Mbpp/791", "solution": "def remove_nested(input: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Validates input is a tuple, removes any element whose type is tuple, and returns the result as a tuple.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: if input is not a tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"input must be a tuple\")\n\n    result = []\n    for item in input:\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple):\n            result.append(item)\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "class SortedList:\n    \"\"\"A lightweight read-only wrapper for list access.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, elements):\n        self._elements = elements\n\n    def length(self) -> int:\n        return len(self._elements)\n\n    def get(self, index: int):\n        \"\"\"Returns the element at the specified index.\"\"\"\n        return self._elements[index]\n\nclass RightInsertionFunction:\n    \"\"\"Computes the 0-based insertion index using right-insertion semantics.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, use_validation: bool = False):\n        self._use_validation = use_validation\n\n    def right_insertion(self, lst, value) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in sorted order.\n        Uses binary search to find the upper bound.\n        \"\"\"\n        sorted_list = SortedList(lst)\n        n = sorted_list.length()\n\n        low = 0\n        high = n\n\n        while low < high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if sorted_list.get(mid) <= value:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid\n        return low\n\ndef right_insertion(lst, value) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in sorted order.\n    assert right_insertion([1,2,4,5],6)==4\n    \"\"\"\n    # Instantiate RightInsertionFunction for delegation as per design.\n    inserter = RightInsertionFunction()\n    return inserter.right_insertion(lst, value)"}
