{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "from bisect import bisect_right\n\ndef last(list, target) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted list.\n    Returns the zero-based index or -1 if the target is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = bisect_right(list, target)\n    if i == 0 or list[i - 1] != target:\n        return -1\n    return i - 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are positive integers (n > 0).\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for n in range(l, r + 1):\n        # Check if n is a natural number (n > 0) and an odd number (n % 2 == 1)\n        if n > 0 and n % 2 == 1:\n            total_sum += n\n    return total_sum"}
